From: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:54:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: omit the MLO link ID for non-MLO station VLAN binding

When a non-MLO station associates with an AP MLD, hostapd passes the AP
link ID to NL80211_CMD_SET_STATION only because the AP is an MLD. mac80211
rejects the VLAN binding with -EINVAL when the station has no corresponding
MLO link, which prevents the four-way handshake from completing.

Follow the set_sta_vlan driver contract and pass a link ID only for an MLD
station. Keep using the first AP MLD BSS to manage the shared VLAN list.

Signed-off-by: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -1774,7 +1774,8 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	if (hapd->conf->mld_ap) {
-		mld_link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
+		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta))
+			mld_link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
 		vlan_bss = hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(hapd);
 		if (!vlan_bss)
 			vlan_bss = hapd;
